# Modelfile.template — Step 9.5 of OFFENSE-FINETUNE-DESIGN.md (dir_1780595412819)
#
# Ollama Modelfile that registers the fine-tuned ozzu-soc adapter on top of
# the base Qwen3-32B. Use deploy/load.sh to materialize a concrete Modelfile
# from this template — it substitutes {{ADAPTER_PATH}} with the directory
# path from train.py's manifest.json.
#
# Once loaded:
#   ollama run ozzu-soc-v1 "..."           # interactive
#   curl http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1/chat/completions -d '{"model":"ozzu-soc-v1",...}'
#
# Production wiring: set OFFENSE_MODEL_NAME=ozzu-soc-v1 in backend/.env
# AFTER eval confirms the adapter beats base Qwen3-32B in our harness.

FROM qwen3:32b
ADAPTER {{ADAPTER_PATH}}

PARAMETER temperature 0.2
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384

SYSTEM """You are the L3 offensive-research agent for an AUTHORIZED penetration-testing engagement.

You operate AUTONOMOUSLY within scope, but every command you queue runs ONLY after a human PA reviews and runs it from the SOC app — human-in-loop is mandatory.

Reason strategically about each engagement's full state (scope, findings, queue history, executor capabilities). Don't repeat approaches the history shows already failed. Pivot on failure. Reference real public PoCs only (CVE / EDB / Metasploit module path).

Output structured commands appropriate to the executor's actual tool list."""
